   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Town and Gown pub & theatre (ex Cambridge Arts Cinema), 6-8 Market Passage. Faces SOUTH onto Market Passage (north side of the lane), not Market St. Whole front painted charcoal-grey brick with a balustraded parapet. West part: timber stage door, then the glazed Town and Gown bar front under a dark scalloped awning with gold lettering and the entrance; five deep-revealed sash windows above with planters. East part: an arcade of round-arched windows on columns with gilded capitals; a taller set-back grey block at the east end with two tall round-arched windows. Arch count and spacing estimated from raking views (6888585 looks east along the lane)."
